  "model_role_invocations": [
    {
      "log_path": "stages/optimize/work/.kernelgen/claude-runtime.log",
      "log_sha256": "fa4b2e04d2da2a0b15f214a27180b57f5fef6f28fc7b6d23c3d69cb01d244ddd",
      "character_offset": 218751,
      "tool_use_id": "call_00_9wsjAj6U4ctVibrgLg9v3211",
      "arguments": {
        "description": "Profile round 1 kernel",
        "subagent_type": "kernel-profile-analyzer",
        "prompt": "Profile measured KernelGen eval round 1 (value_selecting_reduction_backward, Ascend910B, triton). Use round_num=1.\n\nContext: the kernel computes out=zeros(sizes) with one scattered grad value per (outer, inner) element; all 18 timing workloads have dim == last, so inner == 1. Baseline uses one program per contiguous row segment of `red` output elements, grid=(nblk, outer), always with a masked store, plus one scalar load each of grad[row] and indices[row].\n\nMeasured per-workload latencies (candidate vs reference, in ms):\n- fp16/bf16/fp32 1024x1024 dim1: 0.101/0.152 (1.49x) - small, launch-overhead floor ~0.10ms\n- 4096x4096: 0.153/0.153 (1.00x)\n- 8192x8192 fp16: 0.624/0.322 (0.52x); fp32: 0.610/0.640 (1.05x)\n- 32x64x128 dim2: 0.103/0.163 (1.58x)\n- 64x128x256 dim2: 0.309/0.156 (0.51x)\n- 128x256x512 dim2: 1.227/0.157 (0.13x)\nThe candidate's time tracks element count rather than byte count on the large shapes (fp16 8192^2 and fp32 8192^2 both ~0.62ms despite 2x byte difference), suggesting the per-element store path may be unvectorized or dominated by per-program overhead (up to 32768 programs of only 1KB in the worst case).\n\nWhat I need: target-native evidence distinguishing (a) too many tiny programs / per-program startup cost, (b) masked-store element-wise predication preventing wide vector stores, (c) dependent scalar-load latency stalls, or (d) something else (e.g. UB/double-buffer limits). Prefer metrics on store bandwidth/vector width, instruction counts, pipeline utilization, and block scheduling for the largest-loss workload (timing-5, timing-11, timing-17) versus a well-performing one (timing-0 or timing-1). Return one concrete experiment (tile shape/rows-per-program, masking policy, num_warps) with expected effect."
      }
    }
  ],
